WEBVTT

00:07.990 --> 00:08.780
Impossible...

00:13.490 --> 00:14.910
Did you hear me?

00:14.910 --> 00:16.160
Open fire!

00:19.370 --> 00:23.590
Enemy targeting laser has locked on to our stern.

00:23.590 --> 00:25.630
It's firing!

00:25.630 --> 00:27.090
Full output!

00:27.090 --> 00:28.470
Ready to launch!

00:29.050 --> 00:31.050
Bardanos, launch!

00:31.050 --> 00:32.470
Trim 45.

00:32.470 --> 00:33.930
Dive!

01:04.170 --> 01:08.380
A Natura ship that can dive?

01:16.630 --> 01:16.680
LEIJI MATSUMOTO'S

01:16.630 --> 01:16.680
OZMA

01:22.650 --> 01:25.610
You looked over the desert wasteland from above

01:25.610 --> 01:28.820
kareki wo sora de mioroshita

01:25.610 --> 01:28.820
and saw dead trees scattered throughout

01:28.820 --> 01:34.490
aoi tori ga nageki naku to

01:28.820 --> 01:34.490
Blue bird, who knows no sadness

01:35.030 --> 01:37.990
machigai darake no kibou no

01:35.030 --> 01:37.990
I ground my teeth, my hope full of misconceptions

01:37.990 --> 01:42.960
okuba de kanda nigai suna hakidasenai

01:37.990 --> 01:42.960
and couldn't spit out the dreadful sand in my mouth

01:42.960 --> 01:48.090
atoaji wa namida he to toketa

01:42.960 --> 01:48.090
Left was only the salt of tears

01:48.090 --> 01:53.510
aisuru mono sae mamorenai okubyou mono ni

01:48.090 --> 01:53.510
For cowards unable to protect the ones they love

01:53.510 --> 01:59.220
michitarita asa wa konai

01:53.510 --> 01:59.220
no future waits past the dawn of day

01:59.640 --> 02:00.390
Woah

01:59.970 --> 02:00.730
oh

02:00.390 --> 02:01.230
oh!

02:00.770 --> 02:05.730
asu no tobira doko he tsuzuitemo

02:00.770 --> 02:05.730
Wherever the door to the future may lead

02:05.730 --> 02:10.940
haruka misueta me wa nidoto sorasanai

02:05.730 --> 02:10.940
I'll stay focused on what I need to do for it myself

02:10.940 --> 02:12.360
Oh,

02:11.990 --> 02:12.820
woah

02:12.320 --> 02:13.240
oh

02:12.820 --> 02:13.570
oh!

02:13.150 --> 02:17.990
itoshiki kimi no kokoro tataku yo

02:13.150 --> 02:17.990
I will take my place in your heart

02:17.990 --> 02:27.250
itsuka tadashii sekai he kimi wo tsureteyuku kara

02:17.990 --> 02:27.250
because one day I will show you the world we should live in

02:40.100 --> 02:45.020
Episode 2: Diving Limits

02:40.520 --> 02:43.770
Strong magnetic pulses are jamming our sensors.

02:43.770 --> 02:46.270
We are unable to track the enemy ship.

02:46.600 --> 02:49.270
Cut plasma injection to the beam chamber.

02:49.270 --> 02:53.280
Observation teams are to
assess the situation visually.

02:53.280 --> 02:58.780
The sand is obstructing
both visual and long-range infrared.

02:58.780 --> 03:01.950
I'm seeing a cohesion
collapse on the sand ahead.

03:01.950 --> 03:04.370
It's likely a quasi-phase transition field.

03:04.370 --> 03:05.670
A QTF?

03:06.040 --> 03:08.960
All crew are to remain on alert status.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.130
We will move to anti-subterranean mode.

03:12.130 --> 03:14.840
Phonometer Operator, deploy the sonar array.

03:14.840 --> 03:15.630
Yes, sir.

03:18.010 --> 03:21.510
Find them before the LS phase-transition
boundary goes completely underground.

03:21.510 --> 03:22.350
Roger.

03:22.350 --> 03:24.270
Deploying sonar array.

03:32.860 --> 03:34.190
Array online.

03:34.610 --> 03:36.110
Scanning for the enemy.

03:49.540 --> 03:52.880
Looks like they're more than just sand moles.

04:01.430 --> 04:02.970
Depth 300.

04:02.970 --> 04:05.270
Boundary is proceeding underground.

04:07.390 --> 04:08.980
Completing structural check on the ship.

04:08.980 --> 04:10.730
No damage as of yet.

04:10.730 --> 04:12.060
Any sign of pursuit?

04:12.060 --> 04:13.610
I can hear three engines approaching.

04:13.610 --> 04:16.030
They're off the port side, behind us.

04:21.780 --> 04:24.790
Think they freaked out when we just disappeared?

04:24.790 --> 04:25.790
I doubt it.

04:27.960 --> 04:29.790
Cut power to both engines!

04:30.120 --> 04:31.210
We're not running?

04:31.210 --> 04:32.130
Captain!

04:32.130 --> 04:34.380
Their engines are slowing down!

04:34.380 --> 04:37.670
They're not going to stop moving, are they?

04:37.670 --> 04:39.130
As I thought.

04:39.630 --> 04:44.140
They know how to fight under the sand.

04:44.890 --> 04:48.350
They're going to lower
a fishing line and wait us out.

04:53.770 --> 04:56.530
All ships to ready state 4.

04:56.530 --> 04:57.490
Roger.

04:57.490 --> 04:59.490
Slowing primary and side engines.

04:59.740 --> 05:01.070
Speed has dropped.

05:01.070 --> 05:03.990
Engine noise has dropped to 60 dB.

05:05.990 --> 05:09.710
No trace of the enemy's
phonic signature in sector 2.

05:09.910 --> 05:11.870
Expanding the search radius to sectors 1 and 3.

05:11.870 --> 05:12.880
Don't bother.

05:13.330 --> 05:16.000
So, they remain silent?

05:17.170 --> 05:20.340
Arm the enhanced HE rounds with delayed fuses.

05:20.510 --> 05:23.390
Fire in three-point bursts at a five-degree spread.

05:23.390 --> 05:26.310
Aim 1000 meters beyond their last known location.

05:27.100 --> 05:28.100
Sir!

05:35.820 --> 05:37.230
Something's happening!

05:37.230 --> 05:37.940
This is...

05:42.280 --> 05:43.160
Mortars!

05:43.160 --> 05:44.910
They're firing at us!

05:44.910 --> 05:47.290
All hands, prepare for impact!

05:47.580 --> 05:49.660
Pay close attention to where they land!

06:11.680 --> 06:12.480
Crap!

06:12.480 --> 06:14.900
Sam, give us a hand over here!

06:14.900 --> 06:15.860
S-Sure!

06:16.020 --> 06:17.360
You okay?

06:25.820 --> 06:27.240
Mew! Settle down!

06:27.780 --> 06:29.740
Impact points, 1000 meters off the bow.

06:29.740 --> 06:33.080
Looks like they're just firing blindly.

06:33.080 --> 06:34.120
Fool.

06:34.120 --> 06:36.040
That wasn't an attack.

06:36.040 --> 06:38.630
They were confirming our position.

06:39.750 --> 06:43.420
Chief, forward at minimum speed!

06:43.420 --> 06:45.180
Aye aye!

06:45.180 --> 06:47.430
Forward at minimum speed!

06:52.680 --> 06:54.600
Target echo confirmed.

06:54.980 --> 06:56.650
Bring it up on monitor 1.

06:56.650 --> 06:57.690
Sir!

06:58.610 --> 07:02.780
The interference waves are showing
a group delay in the cohesion collapse.

07:02.780 --> 07:07.620
As predicted, the enemy is
deploying a quasi-transition field.

07:07.620 --> 07:10.030
What's the radius of the LS boundary phase?

07:10.030 --> 07:12.290
120 meters.

07:12.290 --> 07:14.460
Bigger than I thought.

07:14.460 --> 07:16.460
The boundary phase is on the move.

07:16.460 --> 07:17.830
3 o'clock.

07:19.460 --> 07:21.210
We've lost the phonic signature.

07:21.210 --> 07:24.220
Continue tracking with the predictive non-linear filter.

07:24.550 --> 07:27.640
Prepare to launch the VLS anchors.

07:27.640 --> 07:30.100
We're attacking with sand anchors?

07:30.430 --> 07:34.270
As long as they're underground,
our beam weapons can't touch them.

07:34.270 --> 07:36.890
But then... Miss Maya...

07:36.890 --> 07:39.980
Our priority now is to stop them from escaping.

07:41.270 --> 07:43.480
I'll take responsibility.

07:46.570 --> 07:47.780
Yes, sir.

07:47.780 --> 07:49.700
Prepare to launch sand anchors.

07:51.700 --> 07:54.000
Loading VLS cells 1, 3, 5 and 7.

07:54.000 --> 07:55.660
Anchor rods loaded.

07:55.660 --> 07:59.630
Targeting the center of the LS boundary phase.

08:01.130 --> 08:02.630
Error compensation complete.

08:03.170 --> 08:05.590
Anchor energy charge complete.

08:05.590 --> 08:06.760
Ready to fire.

08:19.270 --> 08:20.560
Miss Maya.

08:23.860 --> 08:25.400
Fire the anchors!

08:32.450 --> 08:34.040
The enemy has opened fire!

08:34.040 --> 08:35.870
Four... no, six projectiles!

08:35.870 --> 08:37.370
They're firing more!

08:37.370 --> 08:39.250
Are they firing depth charges at us?

08:39.250 --> 08:40.000
No.

08:40.000 --> 08:43.170
Depth charges wouldn't be as loud.

08:43.170 --> 08:44.750
Replay the audio.

08:44.750 --> 08:46.670
Replaying audio.

08:50.180 --> 08:51.640
Engines to full!

08:51.640 --> 08:52.970
Hard to starboard!

08:59.810 --> 09:01.850
We're heading into a reef!

09:01.850 --> 09:04.150
It doesn't matter! Full speed ahead!

09:08.690 --> 09:10.450
Power up the active sonar!

09:10.700 --> 09:12.200
But they'll see us!

09:12.450 --> 09:13.780
Don't worry.

09:13.780 --> 09:15.700
The reef will hide us.

09:16.580 --> 09:17.790
Okay then...

09:17.790 --> 09:19.580
Active sonar online!

09:22.960 --> 09:24.170
A pinger?

09:27.590 --> 09:29.720
Pinger detected at 11 o'clock.

09:29.720 --> 09:31.300
Looks like active sonar.

09:31.300 --> 09:33.090
Display the sound location.

09:37.390 --> 09:38.470
An echo?

09:43.350 --> 09:45.110
30 degrees to starboard.

09:45.110 --> 09:47.110
Head between #3 and #5.

09:47.110 --> 09:48.440
Double the speed of the portside engine!

09:48.440 --> 09:49.740
30 degrees to starboard.

09:49.740 --> 09:51.740
Portside engine to double speed!

09:54.240 --> 09:55.950
45 degrees to starboard!

09:55.950 --> 09:57.370
Head around #5!

09:57.370 --> 09:59.790
45 degrees to starboard.

10:12.090 --> 10:15.180
Use the Doppler differential filter
to pinpoint their location.

10:21.350 --> 10:22.810
Almost past #5.

10:23.980 --> 10:26.860
There's an irregularity at 12 o'clock!

10:26.860 --> 10:28.270
Cut power to both engines!

10:29.230 --> 10:31.440
Reverse engines at full power!

10:31.610 --> 10:32.610
Aye aye!

10:42.790 --> 10:45.120
Calculating final adjustments to targeting.

10:46.380 --> 10:48.380
Transfer data to anchors.

10:55.470 --> 10:57.220
The anchors are going under the sand.

10:59.390 --> 11:01.220
Multiple impacts from above us!

11:21.450 --> 11:24.660
We're detecting echoes from the
anchors and some minor shock waves.

11:24.660 --> 11:27.330
Particle cohesion in the area
ahead of us is returning to normal.

11:27.330 --> 11:29.960
The LS boundary phase is collapsing.

11:30.670 --> 11:32.670
Did we acquire the target?

11:36.760 --> 11:38.760
Any magnetic interference waves?

11:38.760 --> 11:41.390
None as of yet.

11:42.680 --> 11:44.640
So we failed.

11:46.730 --> 11:48.810
They're better than I thought.

12:08.000 --> 12:10.710
Damage report, now.

12:10.960 --> 12:13.090
Did the engines just go quiet?

12:13.090 --> 12:15.300
You think the ship got damaged in all that?

12:15.300 --> 12:17.130
I'll go help.

12:21.970 --> 12:22.970
Maya! You all right?

12:22.970 --> 12:24.430
Say something!

12:24.430 --> 12:25.310
Doctor!

12:31.440 --> 12:33.730
Mimay! Quickly, get her to the infirmary!

12:33.730 --> 12:34.650
Right!

12:40.820 --> 12:42.280
Where is the enemy?

12:42.870 --> 12:46.660
They probably shut down their quasi-transition field.

12:46.660 --> 12:47.870
What?

12:48.040 --> 12:53.000
As long as they hide in the sand,
the anchors will be less effective.

12:53.000 --> 12:55.500
As long as they don't deploy
their LS boundary phase,

12:55.500 --> 13:00.720
then the stone pillars make it
much harder for sonar to detect them.

13:06.310 --> 13:08.770
The engine pipes are partially damaged.

13:08.770 --> 13:10.770
There's also a small breach
on the rear of the stern.

13:10.770 --> 13:13.360
Yam's fixing it now.

13:13.360 --> 13:17.360
Captain, when can we use the quantum
transition generator engine again?

13:22.320 --> 13:25.830
If they stay underground,
they won't be able to dissipate heat.

13:25.830 --> 13:29.160
The temperature will rise,
and the pressure on the ship will...

13:29.160 --> 13:30.500
They're aware of that.

13:31.710 --> 13:33.710
They can do more than just dive.

13:34.880 --> 13:37.880
They're smart.

14:03.950 --> 14:06.740
Captain, at this rate we'll be boiled alive.

14:06.740 --> 14:09.620
Yes, I know.

14:10.580 --> 14:12.870
They've got us pinned down.

14:12.870 --> 14:14.670
Let's attack.

14:14.670 --> 14:18.630
We should be able to get a
homing torpedo up to the surface.

14:18.630 --> 14:22.510
Did you forget that we haven't
finished resupplying yet?

14:24.470 --> 14:27.550
We've got two torpedoes left in the tubes.

14:28.510 --> 14:32.770
Even if both hit,
there'd still be one enemy left.

14:33.810 --> 14:35.440
Damn it!

14:35.440 --> 14:37.980
Are you sure about this, Captain?

14:38.150 --> 14:40.730
Miss Maya is on board that ship.

14:45.910 --> 14:47.370
Her pulse is weak.

14:47.370 --> 14:49.700
Mimay, pass me syringe #3.

14:49.700 --> 14:50.490
Yes, ma'am.

14:50.490 --> 14:53.870
U-Um... I brought some water...

14:53.870 --> 14:54.420
Don't distract her.

15:01.210 --> 15:02.380
Maya!

15:02.380 --> 15:03.720
Hang in there!

15:10.220 --> 15:11.600
So hot...

15:16.650 --> 15:19.270
Internal temperature has exceeded 40 degrees.

15:19.520 --> 15:23.150
Their internal temperature
is about to reach its limit.

15:23.150 --> 15:25.400
And then... Miss Maya...

15:31.410 --> 15:33.330
Hang in there!

15:37.040 --> 15:39.880
She can't take much more of this.

15:45.090 --> 15:47.510
Internal temperature at 48 degrees.

15:51.100 --> 15:52.430
Captain!

16:02.650 --> 16:04.280
Miss Maya...

16:09.070 --> 16:12.620
Internal temperature is about to pass 50 degrees!

16:25.050 --> 16:27.050
C-Captain!

16:30.010 --> 16:32.140
All ships, reverse course.

16:32.510 --> 16:34.520
We're returning to base.

16:34.520 --> 16:35.520
Yes, sir!

16:42.020 --> 16:43.270
What's this?

16:43.520 --> 16:45.400
They're retreating!

16:52.870 --> 16:55.410
Activate quantum transition generator engine.

16:55.700 --> 16:58.080
We're going to periscope depth!

16:58.080 --> 16:59.830
Aye aye!

17:11.220 --> 17:12.300
It's back.

17:12.300 --> 17:14.300
It's back! It's back!

17:48.760 --> 17:49.970
We made it!

17:49.970 --> 17:52.380
They were bigger wimps than I thought!

18:05.400 --> 18:06.480
You're awake!

18:06.860 --> 18:08.110
You all right?

18:08.820 --> 18:09.990
Yes.

18:09.990 --> 18:11.740
You'll be right as rain!

18:11.740 --> 18:13.570
That's good...

18:13.570 --> 18:15.240
No, it's great!

18:15.410 --> 18:16.280
Hell yeah!

18:16.280 --> 18:17.490
Hell-freakin'-yeah!

18:17.490 --> 18:20.290
Hey, you didn't even do anything!

18:20.290 --> 18:22.000
Why are you so happy?

18:22.000 --> 18:23.120
I didn't do anything?

18:23.120 --> 18:25.290
I fanned her and brought her water!

18:25.290 --> 18:26.340
Did you?

18:26.340 --> 18:27.790
More like, you were just in the way.

18:27.790 --> 18:29.170
Like hell I was!

18:29.170 --> 18:29.800
You were!

18:29.800 --> 18:30.840
Was not!

18:46.270 --> 18:50.280
Theseus High Command

18:52.070 --> 18:53.570
Interesting.

18:54.780 --> 18:59.990
Those Natura savages have a ship
that can travel beneath the sand.

19:00.660 --> 19:02.660
I'm sorry, sir.

19:03.080 --> 19:05.540
I underestimated the Natura.

19:05.540 --> 19:07.880
Hateful creatures.

19:07.880 --> 19:10.380
We've been far too kind to them,
it would seem.

19:10.880 --> 19:14.380
It's time they experienced
some pain and suffering instead.

19:15.180 --> 19:19.640
Why did Miss Maya run from us?

19:20.760 --> 19:24.640
She lives in a different time and space than we do.

19:24.640 --> 19:27.730
Her thoughts are always a mystery.

19:27.730 --> 19:30.400
It makes her difficult to babysit.

19:30.980 --> 19:36.410
But she is needed, Gido.

19:36.410 --> 19:40.370
Yes, I will bring her back.

19:40.370 --> 19:42.450
I'm counting on you.

19:43.120 --> 19:45.790
We're running out of time.

20:04.770 --> 20:06.730
Nothin' like this feeling!

20:07.190 --> 20:10.730
Just get some fresh air into you,
and all's right with the world.

20:11.190 --> 20:12.650
Thank you.

20:14.280 --> 20:16.320
It really does feel good.

20:20.740 --> 20:22.120
Oh, right!

20:22.120 --> 20:23.290
Got something awesome to show you.

20:23.290 --> 20:24.240
C'mon, this way!

20:47.060 --> 20:48.770
Bainas, I'm coming in.

20:48.770 --> 20:49.730
Sure.

20:55.940 --> 20:58.200
I was worried today.

20:58.200 --> 20:59.650
What else is new?

21:00.240 --> 21:01.490
What's this?

21:03.070 --> 21:05.950
It's the chart for that girl Sam brought in.

21:08.370 --> 21:11.880
I noticed something odd when I was treating her,
so I took a closer look...

21:15.550 --> 21:16.880
What?

21:16.880 --> 21:19.260
She's no ordinary person...

21:19.550 --> 21:20.930
That girl.

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
shin'ai naru anata he

21:30.100 --> 21:36.530
I ask you, my love,

21:36.530 --> 21:43.910
since when your heart

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
setsunasa to kodoku no aida

21:42.910 --> 21:49.500
has been lost between sorrow and solitude

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
hasamarete kokyuu wo wasureteru

21:49.500 --> 21:56.000
where you lost your grip on reality

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
kanashii uta ni tsutsumarete

21:56.000 --> 22:02.510
All around us we hear songs of lament

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
namida ga ochiru sono mae ni

22:02.510 --> 22:09.020
but before I give in to the tears

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
kizuite anata wo omoinagara

22:08.010 --> 22:14.650
I notice the echoes

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
yasashiku hibiku utagoe ni

22:14.650 --> 22:23.610
of a gentle singing voice around me

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
dareka wo aishite dareka ni aisare

22:23.860 --> 22:31.540
Loving someone and being loved by someone

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
umareta imi ni sotto kizuketa nara

22:30.540 --> 22:36.880
is why we were all born

22:36.880 --> 22:44.380
omoi no mama ni koe wo furishibotte

22:36.880 --> 22:43.170
If you realized that too, put your emotions

22:42.170 --> 22:44.380
into your voice

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
anata mo tsuyoku ai wo utatte hoshii

22:44.380 --> 22:54.520
and please sing of love with all your strength

22:59.940 --> 23:11.950
Next Episode

23:01.030 --> 23:03.570
Why did Theseus come after us?

23:03.570 --> 23:06.490
I heard it's all because of that girl Sam brought in.

23:06.490 --> 23:09.080
Sam'll punch your teeth out
if he hears you say that.

23:09.080 --> 23:10.830
They're fighting over there already!

23:10.830 --> 23:12.230
Let's join in!

23:11.950 --> 23:14.960
Episode 3: A Thousand Years of Doubt

23:12.230 --> 23:13.160
Yeah!
